===Etymology 2===
[[File:Grappling hook 2 (PSF).png|thumb|A [[grappling hook]], which is a type of grapple]]
[[File:FMIB 40673 Grapple.jpeg|thumb|A grapple, or [[grapnel]] anchor]]
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:*grapple<ety:bor<fro:grappil>>|id=hook}}
From {{inh|en|enm|*grapple}}, {{m|enm|*graple}}, from {{derived|en|fro|grappil||a ship's grapple}} (compare {{cog|fro|grappin||hook}}), from {{derived|en|fro|grape}}, {{m|fro|grappe}}, {{m|fro|crape||hook}}, of {{cog|gem}} origin, from {{derived|en|frk|*krappō||hook}}, from {{derived|en|ine-pro|*grep-||hook}}, {{m|ine-pro|*gremb-||crooked, uneven}}, from {{derived|en|ine-pro|*ger-||to turn, bend, twist}}. See further at {{m|en|grape}}. Influenced in some senses by {{m|en|grapple||seize|pos=verb}} (see above).

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[tool]] with [[claw#Noun|claws]] or [[hook#Noun|hooks]] which is used to [[catch#Verb|catch]] or [[hold#Verb|hold]] something.
## {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[device]] consisting of [[iron]] claws, attached to the end of a [[rope]], used for [[grasping]] and [[holding]] an [[enemy]] [[ship]] prior to [[boarding]]; a [[grappling iron]].
## {{lb|en|nautical}} A {{l|en|grapnel|gloss=type of [[anchor]]}}.

