# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[fasten]], as with a [[#Noun|grapple]]; {{lb|en|by extension}} to [[fix]]; to [[join]] [[indissolubly]].
#* {{RQ:Hakluyt Principall Navigations|passage=The gallies were '''grapled''' to the Centurion.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|I|iii|passage='''Grapple''' them to thy soul with hoops of steel.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1901|author=Leonard Charles Smithers|title=Oriental Tales|page=291
|passage={{...}} he provided himself with thieves' tackle and repaired to the house of the vizier in question, where he '''grappled''' a rope ladder with grappling irons to the battlements and climbed up to the roof of the palace .}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914|title=Proceedings of the International Anti-vivisection and Animal Protection Congress, Held at Washington, D.C., December 8th to 11th, 1913|page=51
|passage=[Animals are hung] one by one, by a chain or rope '''grappled''' about a hind ankle, and carried, thus suspended, by an overhead device, to where the sticker stands. As rapidly as he can thrust his knife into the throat he does his work.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=Roger Lichtenberg Simon|title=Raising the dead|isbn=9780394564418
|passage=Then I saw it — a figure swinging just above the arches, hanging from rope '''grappled''' to a lintel of an alcove fifty feet above. It had to be Gordie.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|title=European Conference on Security and Detection - ECOS97, Incorporating the One Day Symposium on Technology Used for Combating Fraud: 28-30 April 1997, Venue, Commomwealth Institute, London
|passage=These toppings impart a swaying motion to anyone climbing a rope '''grappled''' onto them, making climbing difficult. This form of topping is worthy of further study.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Rudy Rodriguez|title=Before There Was|publisher=Lulu.com|isbn=9781105105791|page=448
|passage=He had one of the ropes '''grappled''' around a ledge of a window and the other end  around his ankle for safety purposes, not really expecting it to come into play. He  falls at such an accelerated speed that when the rope becomes taut, it spikes&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Robert E. Waters|title=The Wayward Eight: A Contract to Die For|publisher=Winged Hussar Publishing|isbn=9781620181676
|passage=The men scrambled down the three ropes that had been '''grappled''' up the shaft.}}
#* <!-- or is this "pull" --> '''2015''', Chris Allen, ''Avenger: The Alex Morgan Interpol Spy Thriller Series (Intrepid 3)'', Pan ({{ISBN|9781760082659}})
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[climb]] (whether by means of a grapple and rope, or by hand, etc).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Allen G. Davison|title=The Blessed|isbn=9781469153339|page=149
|passage=Sam quickly geared up and placed the first hook. “I am coming as well,” Alicia announced. {{...}} Sam planted the anchor and then '''grappled''' down as Alicia struggled to move more than a foot or shift down.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Cora Buhlert|title=St. Nicholas of Hell's Kitchen: An Silencer Holiday Story|publisher=Pegasus Pulp Publishing|isbn=9781370889655|page=27
|passage=In cases such as this, the Silencer usually '''grappled''' up the outside of the building. But Rumpus' tower was sixty storeys tall {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Russ Katz|title=The Principal's Daughter|publisher=Dog Ear Publishing|isbn=9781457548925|page=5
|passage=I made haste and '''grappled''' up the next branch, determined to get to the top first.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Edward W. Robertson|title=Freefall
|passage=MacAdams didn't look back to see what they were up to, just ran across the flat roof and '''grappled''' down the other side of the building.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Adair Hart|title=The Earthborn Box Set: Books 1-3|publisher=Quantum Edge Publishing|isbn=9788835378327
|passage=He '''grappled''' up the tree and perched himself on a branch that gave him a good view over the most of the jungle.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Siddhartha Thorat|title=Operation Hellfire|publisher=Sristhi Publishers & Distributors|isbn=9788194241430
|passage=As soon as the snipers had confirmed that the roof was clear, the commandos had '''grappled''' up the five stories. They had used a grappling hook called Tactical  Air Initiated Launch (TAIL) System which could shoot a grappling hook using {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To use a grapple (for example to attempt to find, hook, and raise a net or cable).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1912|title=Sessional Papers - Legislature of the Province of Ontario|page=126
|passage=The following days I spent patrolling the river and '''grappling''' for nets. On Wednesday , 18th July , left Gananoque at 7 a.m.; patrolled down to Rockport, {{...}}}}
#* <!-- move under another sense? --> '''2012''', Jamal Manassah, ''Innovations in Telecommunications'', Elsevier ({{ISBN|9780323145565}}), page 427:
#*: After returning from the cable factory with another load of cable and repeaters, the buoy will be recovered or the rope '''grappled''' for. When the previous section is aboard the ship, transmission tests are made {{...}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To hook and [[raise]] with a grapple.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1861|title=Report of the Joint Committee Appointed by the Lords of the Committee of [Great British] Privy Council for Trade and the Atlantic Telegraph Company|page=263
|passage=The place where the cable got jammed and broken at the bottom was two or three miles from where I '''grappled''' up the cable the first time. I do not, of course,  know for certain whether rocks with crevices exist.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1908|author=New York (State). Court of Appeals|title=New York Court of Appeals. Records and Briefs
|passage=[page 11:] Weston had just '''grappled''' the net, when we saw the light corning up the lake.<br>[page 15:] A. About an hour and a half after dark with Weston I rowed across to this point where the net was set, and he, with a grappling hook, '''grappled''' up the net.}}

